        "title": "Modal Logic: Necessity and Possibility",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Modal logic extends classical logic with operators for **necessity** (box: □) and\n**possibility** (diamond: ◇). Kripke semantics (1963) gives a clean model theory via\n\"possible worlds.\" Modal logic is the parent of temporal logic, epistemic logic,\ndeontic logic, and description logics — all engineering-relevant systems."
